# Phase 5: Outbound Delivery, Meta WhatsApp Cloud API & Lifecycle Handlers

## Overview
Phase 5 implements the outbound messaging layer that proactively delivers recommendations and voice notes back to farmers across Meta WhatsApp Cloud API and Twilio REST API. It introduces customer service window management (24-hour free-form vs. Meta message templates), delivery status callback webhooks (`sent`, `delivered`, `read`, `failed`), worker pipeline Stage 6 integration, and a background reconciliation job for recovering orphaned `inbox/` items.

---

## User Review Required
> [!NOTE]
> All outbound network requests to Meta WhatsApp Cloud API and Twilio REST API use asynchronous HTTP clients (`httpx`) with zero local disk writes and deterministic rate-limit / backoff handling.

---

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Meta WhatsApp Cloud API Client
#### [NEW] [`src/channels/meta/client.py`](file:///e:/Program%20Files/vs%20code/Decillium_farmerProduct/src/channels/meta/client.py)
- **`MetaWhatsAppClient`**:
  - `POST https://graph.facebook.com/{graph_version}/{phone_number_id}/messages` with Bearer auth.
  - **Dual Dispatch**:
    1. Sends formatted recommendation text message.
    2. If `LanguageOutput.media_ref` (audio SAS URL) is present, sends an audio message referencing the SAS URL.
  - **Customer Service Window (24h Rule)**:
    - If `inbound_timestamp` is within 24 hours $\rightarrow$ sends free-form text & audio messages.
    - If outside 24-hour window $\rightarrow$ dispatches approved Meta Message Templates (`price_result_ta`, `clarification_variety_ta`) with typed parameters.
  - **Idempotency & Retries**:
    - Generates and attaches unique `idempotency_key`.
    - Handles 429 rate-limiting with `Retry-After` headers and exponential backoff with jitter.

